// The syntax reference. scripts/build-docs.mjs turns this file into the docs page, llms-full.txt,
// the LLM prompt and the agent skill, and the golden tests check every answer, so the docs can't drift.
// "// ## Title" starts a section; other "//" lines are its description.

// ## Basics
// Type a calculation on any line; its answer appears beside it. Decimals are exact.
2 + 3 × 4 => 14
(2 + 3) × 4 => 20
2^10 => 1,024
10 mod 3 => 1
5! => 120
0.1 + 0.2 => 0.3

// ## Numbers
// Thousands separators, shorthands, other bases and fractions all work.
1,000,000 + 1_000 => 1,001,000
1.5k + 2M => 2,001,500
3bn / 1 million => 3,000
1.5e3 => 1,500
0xFF + 0b1010 => 265
1½ => 1.5

// ## Text and structure
// Words around numbers are ignored, so notes read naturally. Text before a colon is a label. Lines starting with # are headings, and // starts a comment.
3 apples + 2 apples => 5
rent: 1,200 => 1,200
5 plus 3 times 2 => 11
10 divided by 4 => 2.5

// ## Variables
// Name a value with =. Names can have spaces.
monthly rent = 1,200 => 1,200
utilities = 150 => 150
(monthly rent + utilities) × 12 => 16,200

// ## Your own functions and units
// Define a function with name(x) = …, or a unit with 1 name = …. They apply to the lines below.
tip(bill, rate) = bill × rate => (none)
tip($80, 18%) => $14.40
1 sprint = 2 weeks => 2 weeks
3 sprints in days => 42 days
1 dozen = 12 => 12
3 dozen => 36

// ## Previous answers and totals
// prev is the last answer. sum, avg, median, stdev, count, min and max cover the lines since the last heading or blank line. line3 is the answer on line 3. subtotal adds up the lines since the last subtotal, and grand total adds up the subtotals; in the app, double-click a blank line under some answers to add a subtotal.
groceries: 80 => 80
gas: 45 => 45
dinner: 55 => 55
sum => 180
median => 55
avg => 60
prev × 2 => 120

rent: 1,200 => 1,200
power: 80 => 80
subtotal => 1,280
food: 300 => 300
subtotal => 300
grand total => 1,580

// ## Percentages
20% of 50 => 10
50 + 10% => 55
10% off $80 => $72.00
5 as % of 20 => 25%
5 is what % of 20 => 25%
20% of what is 5 => 25

// ## Comparisons and conditions
// Compare with < > <= >= == and !=, and combine with and, or and not. Units and currencies convert before comparing.
5 km > 3 miles => true
0.1 + 0.2 == 0.3 => true
order = $120 => $120.00
if order >= $100 then 10% off order else order => $108.00
0xF0 | 0x0F => 255

// ## Choices
// Options separated by |, with the current one in brackets. In the app, click it to pick the next one. Options can carry values.
transport = car | [train] | fly => train
if transport == train then $80 else $300 => $80.00
fare = car $120 | [train $80] | fly $300 => $80.00

// ## Units
// Convert with in, to or as. Units combine and cancel, and plain numbers take the other side's unit.
5 km in miles => 3.1069 mi
6 ft 2 in in cm => 187.96 cm
72 °F in °C => 22.2222 °C
2 cups in ml => 473.1765 mL
1 GB / 4 MB => 250
60 mph in km/h => 96.5606 km/h
3 m × 4 m => 12 m²
1 m + 20 cm => 1.2 m
12pt in px => 16 px
2 cups flour in g => 240 g

// ## Money
// Currency symbols, codes and names, plus crypto. Rates refresh hourly and keep working offline; these examples use sample rates.
$30 in EUR => €27.00
€20 + $5 => €24.50
hourly rate = $85/h => $85.00/h
37.5 h × hourly rate => $3,187.50
0.01 BTC in USD => $1,000.00

// ## Dates and times
// These examples assume it's Thursday, Jan 15, 2026, 12:00 in UTC.
today + 2 weeks => Thu, Jan 29
next friday at 3pm => Fri, Jan 16, 3:00 PM
days until Dec 25 => 344 days
Jan 31 + 1 month => Sat, Feb 28
3pm + 90 min => 4:30 PM
3 days ago => Mon, Jan 12

// ## Time zones
// Use places (every major city), abbreviations like PST, or offsets like UTC+5:30.
time in Tokyo => 9:00 PM GMT+9
3pm PST in London => 11:00 PM GMT
9:00 EST to CET => 3:00 PM GMT+1

// ## Functions and formats
sqrt(16) + cbrt(27) => 7
round(3.14159, 2) => 3.14
sin(30) => 0.5
log(1000) => 3
2pi => 6.2831853072
255 in hex => 0xFF
1500 in sci => 1.5e3
